# Swan Compiler 2 — SVM Generation
#
# Generate Swan Virtual Machine representation from verified typed IR.
# SVM is Swan's target-independent machine-level compilation representation.
# It is not a runtime virtual machine and does not interpret source programs.
#
# Responsibilities:
# - Lower typed IR operations into a stable SVM instruction set.
# - Assign virtual registers and explicit control-flow edges.
# - Model calls, stack slots, memory, atomics, and ABI boundaries.
# - Keep target-specific register names and instruction encodings out of SVM.
# - Emit relocation and symbol requirements for later target lowering.
#
# Output must pass the SVM verifier. Every opcode must have defined semantics.
# Unknown opcodes and unsupported types are compilation errors.
#
# Implementation status: contract; current IR.swan is an early foundation,
# not a complete SVM instruction selection or machine representation.
